{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "e2f3a4b5-6c7d-4e8f-9a0b-2c3d4e5f6a7b",
    "name": "LedgerOne - Inventory (Reorder Level)",
    "description": "Inventory module (Reorder Level) API collection (Create, Get, Update, List-By-Company, List-By-Warehouse Reorder Level). Reflects the implementation exactly as shipped in apps/api/src/shared/inventory (Ch.42). No DELETE route is mounted for Reorder Level at all this milestone.\n\nCRITICAL GAP \u2014 manual productId fixture required: Reorder Level's create contract takes a real internal numeric productId (a bigint, e.g. \"1\"), never a productUuid. This is a deliberate backend design choice (PK-003 forbids serializing a Product's internal id \u2014 GET /products/:uuid only ever returns uuid), so there is NO HTTP endpoint anywhere in this API that can resolve a productUuid to its internal productId for you. This collection therefore CANNOT self-discover a valid {{productId}} through the API. Before running: connect to local MySQL and run `SELECT id FROM products WHERE uuid = '<real product uuid>'` for a Product that actually exists in your local database, then overwrite the {{productId}} collection variable (defaulted below to \"1\", a placeholder) with that real id. A stale or wrong {{productId}} makes every Reorder Level request in this collection fail with a not-found-style error from the Business layer \u2014 that is expected, not a sign this collection itself is broken.\n\nCRITICAL GAP \u2014 manual warehouseUuid fixture required: {{warehouseUuid}} defaults to an empty string and MUST be filled in with a real Warehouse uuid before running this collection \u2014 create one first via the sibling Warehouse.postman_collection.json (or reuse one already in your local database) and copy its uuid into the {{warehouseUuid}} collection variable. Every request below either sends it in the body or as a required list-query param, so an empty value fails validation immediately.\n\nRoute ordering note: index.ts registers the static /reorder-levels/by-warehouse route BEFORE the /reorder-levels/:reorderLevelUuid param route \u2014 Express matches routes in registration order, so the literal segment must come first or every request for it would instead match :reorderLevelUuid=\"by-warehouse\" (mirroring /units/base-units-before-/units/:unitUuid exactly). This collection exercises both the Company-wide list (bare GET /reorder-levels?companyUuid=) and the Warehouse-scoped list (GET /reorder-levels/by-warehouse?warehouseUuid=) as two distinct, equally-authorized variants.\n\nEvery route requires Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}} AND X-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}} \u2014 a request with no Authorization header 401s with AUTH_MISSING_TOKEN; a missing/malformed X-Tenant-Id header or a malformed request body 422s with VALIDATION_ERROR; unmapped Inventory business errors 422 with INV_DOMAIN_ERROR. {{companyUuid}} defaults to 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111, the shared fixture Company this repo's collections assume exists locally.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
